      "body": "## The problem\r\nI have latest Hassio running in docker on RPi 3B+. I added AsusWRT integration but when I streaming/downloading the amount of transferred data can show maximum of 4GB and then it starts form 0. Looks like counter overflow.   \r\n\r\n## Environment\r\n\r\narch | armv7l\r\ndev | false\r\ndocker | true\r\nhassio | true\r\nos_name | Linux\r\npython_version | 3.7.6\r\ntimezone | Europe/Bratislava\r\nversion | 0.104.3\r\nvirtualenv | false\r\nmode | storage\r\nresources | 0\r\nviews | 4\r\n\r\n## Problem-relevant `configuration.yaml`\r\n```yaml\r\nasuswrt:\r\n  host: 192.168.1.1\r\n  username: admin\r\n  password: !secret asus_router\r\n  sensors:\r\n    - upload\r\n    - download\r\n    - upload_speed\r\n    - download_speed\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\nLink to the download sensor stats [https://drive.google.com/open?id=10Nq5VoGWbOcAzAS7jLQm-ZlzfWGRuRQ9](url)\r\n",
